could bond to an oxygen atom in another water molecule.

45
00:03:16,270 --> 00:03:20,190
依靠斯坦福线性加速器的力量，
Harnessing the power of the Stanford linear accelerator,

46
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:24,480
Anders获得了液态水分子的X射线图像，
Anders took X-ray images of liquid H2O molecules

47
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:28,950
他发现一团团的水分子
and discovered that groups of water molecules

48
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:33,820
就像在跳着美妙同步的舞蹈。
perform an elaborate, synchronized choreography.

49
00:04:00,350 --> 00:04:05,270
一个水分子就像单个舞者，
A single molecule of H2O is like a single swimmer.

50
00:04:05,270 --> 00:04:07,490
既可以自由运动，
Each can move along freely

51
00:04:07,490 --> 00:04:10,660
也可以互相连接起来
or it can link arms with a neighbor

52
00:04:10,660 --> 00:04:13,280
形成刚性结构。
to form a rigid structure.

53
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:17,000
冰点以下，水分子以特定角度连接，
Below freezing, the molecules join at angles

54
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,420
就会占用更大的体积，
and take up more space.

55
00:04:18,420 --> 00:04:21,670
也就可以解释为什么同质量冰的体积比水大。
This is why water expands when it turns to ice.

56
00:04:21,670 --> 00:04:26,660
液态水既包括了自由运动的水分子，
Liquid water contains both freewheeling molecules

57
00:04:26,660 --> 00:04:29,600
也有同时形成的刚性团簇，
and rigid clusters simultaneously.

58
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:32,670
这种结构随温度的变化
These structures form or break apart

59
00:04:32,670 --> 00:04:36,600
形成或分解。
depending on temperature.

60
00:04:36,610 --> 00:04:39,440
但Anders发现水分子也会
But Anders discovered that water molecules

61
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:41,140
基于溶解在水中的物质
also change their routine

62
00:04:41,140 --> 00:04:43,810
改变自己的运动方式。
depending on what's mixed in with them.

63
00:04:43,810 --> 00:04:46,280
假如这个就是氯化钠晶体，
So, here I have a sodium chloride crystal.

64
00:04:46,280 --> 00:04:49,350
也是加入食物中的食盐，
This is just ordinary salt like you have in your food,

65
00:04:49,350 --> 00:04:51,370
海洋中也有大量的氯化钠。
what we have in the ocean.

66
00:04:51,370 --> 00:04:53,570
这就给你举个例子。
So, if you look at this example.

67
00:04:55,660 --> 00:04:58,830
当把盐加入到
When ordinary table salt comes into contact

68
00:04:58,830 --> 00:05:01,460
有着刚性构象的水分子中，
with a rigid formation of water molecules,

69
00:05:01,460 --> 00:05:06,720
这种构象就崩解了。
that formation breaks apart.

70
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:10,200
这就创造了更多的自由水分子
This creates more free-floating molecules

71
00:05:10,210 --> 00:05:12,170
将食盐晶体溶解，
that break salt crystals apart

72
00:05:12,170 --> 00:05:16,390
并将食盐分子融入整个水体中。
and spread them throughout the body of water.

73
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:19,880
其他化学物质与水有着不同的反应，
Other chemicals have a different effect.

74
00:05:19,880 --> 00:05:23,930
假如这是强带电离子物质，
So, here we have a very strongly or highly charged ion.

75
00:05:23,940 --> 00:05:27,240
比如镁或铝离子，
This can be like magnesium or aluminum ion.

76
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:29,020
然后我们把它放在水中，
And then we're going to throw in this,

77
00:05:29,030 --> 00:05:32,410
水分子在其周围就会形成冰样结构，
and we're going to form an ice-like structure around it.

78
00:05:35,900 --> 00:05:42,000
这样水分子就将离子锁住。
Water molecules lock around the ion and hold it in place.

79
00:05:46,840 --> 00:05:53,010
对于我们来说，一杯水看似静止又毫无生气，
To us, a glass of water seems still and lifeless.

80
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:58,050
但是在分子层面，它存在着强烈活性，
But on the molecular scale, it is pulsing with activity.

81
00:05:58,050 --> 00:06:01,640
水分子结构的改变
Water changes its molecular structure

82
00:06:01,640 --> 00:06:05,060
每秒会发生1万亿次。
around 1 trillion times per second.

83
00:06:05,060 --> 00:06:08,650
一旦水分子结构改变，
Whenever the molecular structure of water changes,

84
00:06:08,650 --> 00:06:12,430
宏观上水的化学性质也随即改变，
the overall chemical properties of water also change.

85
00:06:12,430 --> 00:06:17,100
地球上只有水才有这种特性。
No other liquids on earth can do this.

86
00:06:17,110 --> 00:06:20,210
水分子对温度变化的响应，
Water molecules respond to temperature

87
00:06:20,210 --> 00:06:23,080
以及对其接触的化学物质的响应，
and the chemicals they come in contact with

88
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:28,620
就像水能够意识到周围环境一样。
almost as if the water is aware of its surroundings.

89
00:06:28,620 --> 00:06:33,790
对于Anders来说，化学物质和生物之间的界线
For Anders, this property blurs the distinction

90
00:06:33,790 --> 00:06:38,140
因水的这种性质而模糊了。
between a chemical and a living thing.

91
00:06:38,140 --> 00:06:40,340
有人可能也认为
Some people might think

92
00:06:40,350 --> 00:06:43,130
这杯水是活的，
that a glass of water could be alive.

93
00:06:43,130 --> 00:06:44,900
我个人对生命的理解是
My personal view of life

94
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:47,470
生命需要与
is that it's related to something

95
00:06:47,470 --> 00:06:50,740
某种程度的意识有所联系，
that has consciousness on some sort of level,

96
00:06:50,740 --> 00:06:54,410
问题在于，水是否有意识？
and the question is if that is the case with water,

97
00:06:54,410 --> 00:06:57,190
我们无法直接回答“有”还是“没有”。
and we -- we can't say "yes" or "no."

98
00:06:58,660 --> 00:07:02,500
无论这杯水是不是活的，
Whether or not a glass of water is alive,

99
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:05,250
水仍是支撑我们所知的
water itself is still the essence

100
00:07:05,250 --> 00:07:07,370
所有生命的基本元素。
of all life that we know of.

101
00:07:07,370 --> 00:07:10,660
人体中60%都是水，
About 60% of your body is water.

102
00:07:10,660 --> 00:07:14,350
细胞和DNA存在于水中，
Cells with your DNA call it home,

103
00:07:14,350 --> 00:07:18,670
还有你身上的大约1000种细菌。
along with about 1,000 unique species of bacteria.

104
00:07:18,670 --> 00:07:22,550
海洋生态系统中水也占了大部分，
The ocean ecosystem is also mostly water,

105
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:26,010
供养了数百万种生命，
and home to millions of life forms.

106
00:07:26,010 --> 00:07:29,840
那么海水和其中的各种生物，
Could ocean water and the life that calls it home

107
00:07:29,850 --> 00:07:32,200
算是共同存在的生物吗？
collectively be a living thing?

108
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:36,730
这是否可能是一种巨型生命形式呢？
Is a life form that large even possible?

109
00:07:41,990 --> 00:07:46,490
进化生物学家Gustavo Caetano-Anolles
Evolutionary biologist Gustavo Caetano-Anolles

110
00:07:46,500 --> 00:07:48,210
认为可能是这样的。
suspects it was.

111
00:07:48,210 --> 00:07:51,700
他的研究追溯到了最早的生命形式，
He's tracking down earth's first life form,

112
00:07:51,700 --> 00:07:55,300
一种处于进化树最基层的生物。
the creature at the root of the tree of life.

113
00:07:55,300 --> 00:07:58,140
进化树是一个层级结构，
A tree of life is an hierarchical structure.

114
00:07:58,140 --> 00:08:00,890
这说明如果你往回走，
That means that if you travel back in time,

115
00:08:00,890 --> 00:08:05,180
直到发现一种生物，
you are traveling to an organism that at some point

116
00:08:05,180 --> 00:08:09,270
它身上会体现出未来所有生物的特征。
embedded all the diversity that was generated later on.

117
00:08:11,900 --> 00:08:15,720
这就是地球生命最后的共同祖先，简写为“LUCA”。
【诶？Miku呢？】
And this is the last universal common ancestor, or LUCA.

118
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:19,780
LUCA算是对地球上
LUCA is the scientific nickname

119
00:08:19,780 --> 00:08:22,200
最早出现的物种的昵称，
for the first species on earth.

120
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:25,530
它存活于35亿年前，
It lived about 3.5 billion years ago,

121
00:08:25,530 --> 00:08:29,570
是今天所有生物的共同祖先。
and is common ancestor to all life today.

122
00:08:29,570 --> 00:08:34,010
LUCA细胞可能遍布原始海洋之中，
LUCA cells likely filled the primordial ocean,

123
00:08:34,010 --> 00:08:37,410
没有任何其他物种与之竞争。
unhindered by any competing organism.

124
00:08:37,410 --> 00:08:41,350
LUCA已经灭绝几十亿年了，
LUCA has been extinct for billions of years.

125
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:47,600
但是Gustavo认为他能够通过
But Gustavo believes he can reconstruct

126
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:49,470
研究当今的生命结构的细节
what its cells looked like

127
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:53,030
来重建LUCA细胞的样貌。
by studying the details of life's machinery today.

128
00:08:53,030 --> 00:08:56,150
对于Gustavo来说，
For Gustavo, finding the elements

129
00:08:56,150 --> 00:08:58,480
找出构成最原始生命的基本要素，
essential to the earliest life form

130
00:08:58,480 --> 00:09:01,770
就像是探究最早的自行车是如何工作的。
is like figuring out how the very first bicycle worked.

131
00:09:03,370 --> 00:09:05,770
自行车是不断变化的，
Bikes are permanently changing.

132
00:09:05,770 --> 00:09:08,130
每十年都有新的发展，
Every 10 years, we have new developments,

133
00:09:08,130 --> 00:09:12,210
会加上新的结构和新的电子设备。
new mechanisms, new electronics added to them.

134
00:09:12,210 --> 00:09:17,080
但是自行车的基本结构是相对固定的。
In contrast, the structure of a bike is rather permanent.

135
00:09:17,090 --> 00:09:21,260
现代自行车有着非常精密的传动装置
Bikes today come with a variety of sophisticated gears

136
00:09:21,260 --> 00:09:22,960
以及高科技材料，
and high tech materials,

137
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:26,260
但仍有着共同的基本结构，
but all share common, essential structures.

138
00:09:26,260 --> 00:09:29,150
没有它们，自行车就不能运行。
Without them, a bike cannot function.

139
00:09:30,130 --> 00:09:34,430
在第一辆自行车上，我能够找到车座、
In the first bike, I would find a seat,

140
00:09:34,440 --> 00:09:36,400
踏板、车轮，
pedals, wheels,

141
00:09:36,410 --> 00:09:39,690
因为这些东西在我现在研究的自行车上
because these seem to be common to all bikes

142
00:09:39,690 --> 00:09:41,470
仍然存在。
that I can study today.

143
00:09:41,480 --> 00:09:45,150
对于这些基本部件的研究，
With a list of these fundamental parts,

144
00:09:45,150 --> 00:09:49,280
Gustavo重建出了自行车的
Gustavo can reconstruct the last universal common ancestor

145
00:09:49,290 --> 00:09:52,200
共同祖先--
of bicycles --

146
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:54,370
古董自行车...
the penny-farthing...

147
00:09:56,820 --> 00:10:01,930
...第一个被称作自行车的设备。
...the first machine to be called a bicycle.

148
00:10:01,930 --> 00:10:05,350
它有车座、脚踏板和车轮，
It had a seat, pedals, and wheels,

149
00:10:05,350 --> 00:10:09,600
但不需要链条或齿轮等传动装置。
but didn't need a chain or gears to move.

150
00:10:09,610 --> 00:10:15,860
Gustavo将这一原理应用于对LUCA的研究中，
Gustavo applied this same philosophy to his hunt for LUCA.

151
00:10:15,860 --> 00:10:17,950
通过将上千种生物的基因结构
By comparing the fossil records

152
00:10:17,950 --> 00:10:21,230
与化石记录进行比较，
to the genetic record of thousands of organisms,

153
00:10:21,230 --> 00:10:24,120
Gustavo得知了哪些蛋白质存在于
Gustavo worked out which proteins existed

154
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:26,950
35亿年前。
about 3.5 billion years ago.

155
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:30,570
他列出了LUCA所需的
He generated a list of fundamental parts

156
00:10:30,580 --> 00:10:32,710
所有基本部件。
that LUCA must have had.

157
00:10:32,710 --> 00:10:35,330
让他惊讶的是，他发现
To his surprise, he discovered

158
00:10:35,330 --> 00:10:38,830
LUCA和当今的生物非常不同，
that unlike all life we know of today,

159
00:10:38,830 --> 00:10:43,250
LUCA很可能不具备密封性良好的细胞壁。
【细胞膜更贴切，但尊重原意还是译为细胞壁吧】
LUCA probably did not have a well-sealed cell wall.

160
00:10:43,260 --> 00:10:45,510
很可能
It is quite possible

161
00:10:45,510 --> 00:10:47,890
LUCA的细胞壁是多孔的，
that the cell walls of LUCA were porous,

162
00:10:47,890 --> 00:10:51,350
这就允许不同LUCA细胞之间
and that they would allow for fast exchange

163
00:10:51,350 --> 00:10:56,850
进行遗传物质的快速交换，
between the different LUCA cells of genetic information,

164
00:10:56,850 --> 00:10:59,740
包括一些细胞结构的交换。
and also of actual machinery.

165
00:10:59,740 --> 00:11:04,610
我们把LUCA细胞当做古董自行车，
Think of a LUCA cell as a penny-farthing bicycle.

166
00:11:04,610 --> 00:11:08,160
由于其细胞壁布满了孔洞，
Because its cell wall was full of holes,

167
00:11:08,160 --> 00:11:12,280
LUCA细胞的重要组成部分可以流动。
important parts could come loose and float away.

168
00:11:12,280 --> 00:11:16,340
而水分子则与脱离的部分相互作用，
Water molecules could, however, react to this escaped part

169
00:11:16,340 --> 00:11:19,010
在其周围形成保护层，
and form a supportive mold around it

170
00:11:19,010 --> 00:11:21,840
直到这部分被另一个LUCA细胞捕获，
until it drifts into another LUCA cell

171
00:11:21,840 --> 00:11:24,910
那么这部分就又重新利用了。
where that part could be reused.

