我们把寄生虫当做指示灯，
We think of each parasite as a little light.

683
00:41:17,690 --> 00:41:19,370
绿灯代表一种寄生虫，
The green light is one species,

684
00:41:19,370 --> 00:41:22,080
红灯代表另外一种。
and the red light is another species.

685
00:41:22,080 --> 00:41:25,300
然后观察它们
We can then watch them follow this linear path

686
00:41:25,300 --> 00:41:27,300
看它们在食物链中的位置,
up the food chain,

687
00:41:27,300 --> 00:41:30,420
每处它们停留的地方
stopping along the way at the various stops

688
00:41:30,420 --> 00:41:33,640
都表示着宿主的情况。
which reflect the different hosts in their life cycles.

689
00:41:33,640 --> 00:41:37,390
如果寄生虫的数量开始减少，
If populations of parasites begin to disappear,

690
00:41:37,390 --> 00:41:41,730
就说明食物链出了问题，
it could mean that there are breaks in the food chain,

691
00:41:41,730 --> 00:41:45,730
生态环境正在趋向崩溃。
and the environment is headed towards catastrophe.

692
00:41:45,730 --> 00:41:49,320
David曾经通过测量寄生虫种群数量
David monitors the ecological health

693
00:41:49,320 --> 00:41:51,890
对加拿大地区的河流和湖泊
of the rivers and lakes across Canada

694
00:41:51,890 --> 00:41:54,520
进行了生态系统健康程度的监控。
by surveying the parasite populations.

695
00:41:54,530 --> 00:41:59,530
而对海洋来说这会是一项艰难的任务，
Doing the same for the ocean will be a herculean task,

696
00:41:59,530 --> 00:42:03,170
但David希望有一天能够实现。
but David hopes one day to take it on.

697
00:42:03,170 --> 00:42:07,120
海洋是一个巨大的栖息地，
The ocean is such a vast habitat.

698
00:42:07,120 --> 00:42:09,410
这里是探索未知的另一侧，
It's another frontier.

699
00:42:09,410 --> 00:42:11,880
探索海洋所需要的付出相当于
You would need the kind of resources you need

700
00:42:11,880 --> 00:42:12,930
探索月球的成本。
to go to the moon.

701
00:42:12,930 --> 00:42:15,080
科学家们尚不清楚
Scientists don't know

702
00:42:15,080 --> 00:42:17,910
海洋中究竟有什么，
what's really out there in the sea,

703
00:42:17,920 --> 00:42:21,550
也没人知道到什么程度
and no one knows how far the ocean can be pushed

704
00:42:21,550 --> 00:42:23,350
海洋才会发动毁灭性的打击。
before catastrophe strikes.

705
00:42:29,610 --> 00:42:33,230
海洋也许有着生存的意愿，
The ocean may have a will to live,

706
00:42:33,230 --> 00:42:37,620
也许会不假思索的驱逐无礼的人类，
or it may react unthinkingly to our insults.

707
00:42:37,620 --> 00:42:41,070
不论怎样，我们都不应该低估
Either way, we should not underestimate

708
00:42:41,070 --> 00:42:44,910
它凌驾于地球上所有生命的力量。
the power it has over all life on the planet.

709
00:42:44,910 --> 00:42:48,710
包含着其中数以百万的生命，
With its millions of species, the ocean might be

710
00:42:48,710 --> 00:42:52,300
海洋可能是地球上迄今为止最奇妙的，
the most remarkable creature we'll ever meet,

711
00:42:52,300 --> 00:42:56,400
最大最古老的生命。
the largest and oldest life form on earth.

